  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "DOLLARDE and DOLLARFR scale by 10^ceil(log10(d)) and keep truncated fraction as binary64",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20430, DOLLARDE and DOLLARFR truncate fraction toward zero as binary64 (avoiding 32-bit integer saturation, so DOLLARDE(1.5, 1e10) returns 1.5), reject negative fraction with #NUM! and truncated 0 with #DIV/0!, and scale the fractional part using 10^ceil(log10(d)) rather than 10^(digit count). Consequently, any power-of-10 denominator (1, 10, 100, 1e10) equals its scale and leaves the input number unchanged. All 4,847 DOLLARDE and 3,641 DOLLARFR full-bank rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-5-20260924/answers/answers-w1115-dollarde.json.gz and cache/oracle-20430/build-20430/DOLLARFR.jsonl.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430); 4,847/4,847 DOLLARDE and 3,641/3,641 DOLLARFR full-bank rows match.",
